    content:
      "<div><p>The trend of influencers has skyrocketed in the past few years. Aside from celebrity endorsements, organisations are now giving equal importance to <strong>influencer marketing </strong>, thus increasing its revenue to $16.4 billion in 2022. This year, social media has witnessed a myriad of influencer-led strategies,but one that Cinthol employed received favourable feedback, garnered over 7 million viewers and isstill one of the most effective <strong>influencer marketing </strong> plans ever.</p><h5><strong>An overview of Cinthol&#39;s marketing approach</strong></h5> <p>One of the most well-known and popular brands in the Godrej Consumer Products Limited portfolio,Cinthol, was known for several things, one of which was its distinctive brand voice that resonates with the general audience.</p><p>Throughout its six decades as a household name, the brand has launched numerous marketing campaigns that have featured iconic personalities like Sharukh Khan, Hrithik Roshan, and Virat Kohli.Some of these commercials are still engraved in the memories of millennials as a lasting nostalgia.</p><h5><strong>The reason behind the success of Cinthol’s marketing approaches</strong></h5><p>One of the many factors contributing to Cinthol&#39;s marketing campaign&#39;s success is its emphasis on relevancy and the constant adoption of cutting-edge technologies. They are regarded as a successful brand since they consistently create advertisements based on what the public finds fascinating.</p><p>To continue their winning streak, Cinthol did what they always do: they embraced current marketing  trends.They revised their strategy and partnered with Clan Connect, a well-known influencer marketing agency, to launch campaigns to promote their brand.</p><h5>Cinthol’s influencer marketing strategy</h5><p>Given the history of Cinthol&#39;s marketing strategy, which has always been centred on adventure, the brand decided to work with influencers who enjoy the experience. The campaign&#39;s goal was to cultivate a community of adventure lovers and explorers that live up to the tagline &quot;Alive is Awesome.&quot;</p><p>The goal was to entice the zest for adventure among millennials and fellow adventure enthusiasts while establishing brand relevance among a young audience. The brand decided to produce a series of videos called &quot;Cinthol Alive Adventures&quot;, starring India&#39;s top social media influencers to elicit interest among social media users. Each episode spotlights entertaining conversations with these travel influencers as they recall their most thrilling adventures.</p></div><h5><strong>The process of the marketing campaign</strong></h5><p>Identifying and engaging with relevant influencers is the first step in moving forward with the campaign. Given that there are between 3.2 million and 37.8 million influencers worldwide across all social media platforms, it can be challenging to find a notable influencer of a relevant niche who fulfils the needed categories. Therefore, Cinthol collaborated with Clan Connect, an <strong>influencer marketing platform</strong>that helps locate relevant influencers.</p><p>The marketing teams enlisted many influencers with similar mindsets and a passion for adventure via the Clan Connect tool. Through the use of insightful data offered by the cutting-edge Tech platform, the list of influencers was analysed and narrowed down based on variables such as reach, relevancy, content quality, and engagement.</p><h5><strong>Launching the marketing campaign</strong></h5><p>Cinthol launched the mini web series after selecting a group of 37 well-known adventure and travel influencers, and it quickly gained millions of viewers.</p><p>Then, Cinthol launched #CintholAliveAdventures, a user-generated content (UGC) digital campaign,as a wrap-up to their digital campaign after the strategy had begun to yield results. The #CintholAliveAdventures, goal is to provide a space for people to relive past memorable adventures in exchange for Virtual Reality (VR) headsets.</p><h5><strong>The outcome of the marketing campaign</strong></h5><p>Cinthol&#39;s &quot;Cinthol Alive Adventures&quot; campaign reached over 7 million people, generated 56 million impressions, received 740+ entries for the user-generated content campaign, and experienced a 29% increase in engagement as a response to the buzz generated by the influencer marketing strategy. Ultimately, the campaign was a triumph.</p><p>With the aid of the <strong>influencer marketing company </strong>Clan Connect, brands can swiftly list influencers relevant to their brand, promote their brand message, and enrich their brand&#39;s reputation.</p>",
