    newsCategory: "",
    newsPostedBy: "By Clan Team",
    content:
      "<p>The social media ecosystem is replete with content creators generating high-quality content tailored to the needs and preferences of their target audiences. While almost every social media user is considered a content creator today, those who consistently post relevant content become great influencers. In fact, influencer marketing has grown so massively that it is now a lucrative career option with no age barriers.</p><p>This profession offers mind-blowing opportunities for influencer marketing brand collaborations with creators. These influencers add exceptional value to their consumers through their authentic and organic content, be it funny or educational. Brands have realized their potential and are moving from traditional celebrities to nano (1K to 10K followers) and micro-influencers (10K to 50K followers) to drive faster growth.</p><p>Research says 61% of consumers rely on influencer recommendations compared to 38% of those who trust branded content. Evidently, 60% of marketers believe influencer-generated content performs better and drives more engagement against branded posts. In the Indian context, over a third of brands have increased their budget for social media influencers by 2X in recent years.</p><p>These statistics underline the growth potential of influencer marketing in the current business landscape. This blog discusses the top three trends in this space that are expected to gain relevance in the coming times.</p><h5><strong>Video content will thrive</strong></h5><p>Smartphones have undoubtedly become a mainstream device for watching all types of videos, be it short-form like reels or long-form like movies and series. From a creator's POV too, mobiles are like a one-man army that can perform all the activities from shooting a video to editing, posting, and sharing it.</p><p>As a result, brands are also collaborating with influencers to create branded video content, convincing consumers to buy. Some of the top video platforms leveraged by influencers are YouTube, Instagram and Facebook.</p><h5><strong>Live promotions will continue to gain relevance</strong></h5><p>The live feature, now available on almost every platform, be it YouTube, Instagram, or LinkedIn, is widely being leveraged by influencers to promote branded content and, in some cases, personal content like live courses or workshops.</p><p>Now, these platforms also allow people to shop live using livestream shopping tools. For instance, Instagram enables consumers to buy products directly via Instagram Live. In fact, shoppers, through this format, can learn and discover more about the product in an immersive manner before buying it.</p><h5><strong>Scope for more professional content</strong></h5><p>As influencer-related content becomes more saturated, it will become imperative for brands to look at more innovative ways to create noise and drive reach. Influencers can do this by focusing on a particular niche and crafting content within that space accordingly. </p><p>Moreover, to maintain relevance in the ever-evolving social media market, influencers must learn the new features and acclimatize with the new formats of these platforms to create viral content. All these inevitable changes will push influencers to think more innovatively and build more professional content with in-depth insights.</p><p>With influencer marketing gaining traction, many influencing marketing platforms have also emerged to cater to the needs of brands. ClanConnect, for instance, is a leading influencer marketing agency in India adept at planning and tracking influencer marketing campaigns. This influencing marketing company is equipped with the right tools and data to help make informed decisions, enabling brands to run successful influencing marketing campaigns.</p><p>The creator economy has grown immensely in India, and now with more and more creators taking up entrepreneurship roles, it is essential for brands to look for more conscious and mindful collaborations if they want to thrive in today's digital-first world. This is where players like ClanConnect chip in with the expertise to catapult brands to new heights.</p>",
